values under question go to the core of our society.

Already, New Zealand "60 Minutes" is proposing a segment on the pornography
and other "nasties" that may be found on Internet, which could 
also be shown on the Australian program.

The inquiry at UNSW has an opportunity to assert good sense and show a
positive example for the value of freedom of expression.

As I argued in the letter in the Australian published today (Tuesday July 20),
we do not need laws to control the electronic network.



