discriminatory and what warrants action?  Must the common law be
burdened with superficially offensive comments which amount to nothing?

What kind of society do you want -- one in which people know how to talk
freely (and handle conflicts openly), or one in which people refrain
from talking for fear of stepping on others' toes?


Incidentally, which new federal laws did you have in mind? 
(The Racial Vilification Act is a state law enacted in Western Australia. It is a bad law and ought to be repealed.)



>The above are personal opinions.  I am not involved in the above matters.
